le=\"Langfuse\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://www.jaegertracing.io\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/jaeger\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Jaeger\" title=\"Jaeger\" /></a>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| **Local and Remote**             | <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Random-access_memory\"><img src=\"https://api.iconify.design/lucide/memory-stick.svg?color=%23888888\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"RAM\" title=\"RAM\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File_system\"><img src=\"https://api.iconify.design/lucide/hard-drive.svg?color=%23888888\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Disk\" title=\"Disk\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/File_System_API/Origin_private_file_system\"><img src=\"https://api.iconify.design/lucide/folder-lock.svg?color=%23888888\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"OPFS\" title=\"OPFS\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secure_Shell\"><img src=\"docs/images/ssh-logo.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"SSH\" title=\"SSH\" /></a>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n\nAgents reach it through the Python and TypeScript SDKs, the `mirage` CLI, or a real\nmountpoint over FUSE and FSKit, then work it with the unix tools they already know,\nlike `ls`, `grep`, `find` and `jq`.\n\n## Virtual Command Line Tool\n\nThese command line tools are virtualized: [Mirage](https://www.strukto.ai/mirage) answers `git`, `slack` or `ntn`\nitself, so an agent drives the service without that program being installed on the\nmachine. Each one mimics the real tool, so an agent that knows the CLI needs nothing\nnew. Because they are virtual, the same tool can be installed more than once under\ndifferent names, each with its own credentials, so every agent gets exactly the\naccounts it is given.\n\n|                   | CLIs                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Code**          | <a href=\"https://git-scm.com\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/git\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"git\" title=\"git\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://cli.github.com\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/github/181717/e6edf3\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"gh\" title=\"gh\" /></a>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| **Communication** | <a href=\"https://slack.com\"><img src=\"https://api.iconify.design/logos/slack-icon.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"slack\" title=\"slack\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://discord.com\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/discord\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"discord\" title=\"discord\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://github.com/pimalaya/himalaya\"><img src=\"assets/icons/himalaya.png\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"himalaya\" title=\"himalaya\" /></a>                                                                                                                            |\n| **Work and Data** | <a href=\"https://linear.app\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/linear\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"linear\" title=\"linear\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://www.notion.so\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/notion/000000/e6edf3\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"ntn\" title=\"ntn\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://workspace.google.com\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/google\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"gws\" title=\"gws\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://huggingface.co\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/huggingface\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"hf\" title=\"hf\" /></a> |\n\n## Virtual Runtime\n\nRuntimes are virtualized the same way, and not only for coding languages. Any\ncommand on the line can be redirected to a configured runtime, so Python might\nrun in-process with [Monty](https://pydantic.dev/articles/pydantic-monty) while\nanother command, say `kubectl`, is sent to a remote machine over SSH. Which runtime\nserves a given line can be decided by a\n[scripted runtime router](https://docs.mirage.strukto.ai/home/policy/route-runtime).\n\n|                | Runtimes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Python**     | <a href=\"https://pydantic.dev/articles/pydantic-monty\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/pydantic\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Monty\" title=\"Monty\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://wasi.dev\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/webassembly\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"WASI CPython on wasmtime\" title=\"WASI CPython on wasmtime\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://pyodide.org\"><img src=\"assets/icons/pyodide.svg\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Pyodide\" title=\"Pyodide\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://pypi.org/project/sandlock/\"><img src=\"docs/images/sandlock-logo.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"sandlock\" title=\"sandlock\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://www.python.org\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/python\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Host CPython\" title=\"Host CPython\" /></a>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| **JavaScript** | <a href=\"https://docs.mirage.strukto.ai/home/setup/runtime/quickjs\"><img src=\"assets/icons/quickjs.png\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"QuickJS, serving node and js\" title=\"QuickJS, serving node and js\" /></a> <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/javascript\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"JavaScript\" title=\"JavaScript\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.typescriptlang.org\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/typescript\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"TypeScript\" title=\"TypeScript\" /></a>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| **Machines**   | <a href=\"https://www.docker.com\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/docker\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Docker\" title=\"Docker\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://e2b.dev\"><img src=\"docs/images/e2b-logo.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"E2B\" title=\"E2B\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://www.daytona.io\"><img src=\"docs/images/daytona-logo.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Daytona\" title=\"Daytona\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://smolmachines.com\"><img src=\"docs/images/smolvm-logo.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"smolVM\" title=\"smolVM\" /></a> <a href=\"https://microsandbox.dev\"><img src=\"docs/images/microsandbox-logo.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Microsandbox\" title=\"Microsandbox\" /></a> <a href=\"https://github.com/apple/container\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/apple/000000/e6edf3\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Apple Container\" title=\"Apple Container\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secure_Shell\"><img src=\"docs/images/ssh-logo.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"SSH\" title=\"SSH\" /></a> |\n\n## Security\n\nA profile decides what a session may run and what it may see. Commands are governed\nby customizable `allow`, `ask` and `deny` rules, and paths by `hide` and `show`, so a\nhidden file is not merely unreadable but absent from the filesystem the agent sees.\nFor anything those rules cannot express, a profile can name a policy script that runs\nat the gate on every command and answers allow, deny or ask itself, though like every\nrule it can only restrict and never grant. Separately, a host can register its own\npolicies on the [policy engine](https://docs.mirage.strukto.ai/home/policy/policies), an\nordered stack the workspace consults on every command, VFS op and session write. See\nthe [policy docs](https://docs.mirage.strukto.ai/home/policy/overview).\n\n## Authentication\n\nCredentials and authentication integrate with the stores secrets already live in,\nincluding AWS Secrets Manager, 1Password, Auth0 and dotenv, so an environment variable\nin Mirage can resolve straight to a credential held in one of them.\n\n|              | Sources                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Built in** | <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Environment_variable\"><img src=\"assets/icons/terminal.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Environment\" title=\"Environment\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.dotenv.org\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/dotenv\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"dotenv\" title=\"dotenv\" /></a> <a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/secrets-manager/\"><img src=\"https://api.iconify.design/logos/aws-secrets-manager.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"AWS Secrets Manager\" title=\"AWS Secrets Manager\" /></a> |\n| **Custom**   | <a href=\"https://1password.com\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/1password\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"1Password\" title=\"1Password\" /></a> <a href=\"https://auth0.com\"><img src=\"https://cdn.simpleicons.org/auth0\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Auth0\" title=\"Auth0\" /></a>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n\n## Installation\n\n- **Python** ≥ 3.12 for the `mirage-ai` package and the `mirage` CLI\n- **Node.js** 22.20+ on Node 22, 24.12+ on Node 24, or 25+ for the TypeScript SDK\n\n### Python\n\n```bash\nuv add mirage-ai              # installs the `mirage` library and the `mirage` CLI binary\nuv add 'mirage-ai[openai]'    # OpenAI Agents adapter; each agent framework is an extra\n```\n\n### TypeScript\n\n```bash\nnpm install @struktoai/mirage-node      # Node.js servers and CLIs\nnpm install @struktoai/mirage-browser   # browser / edge runtimes\nnpm install @struktoai/mirage-vercel    # Vercel AI adapter; each agent framework has its own package\n```\n\nBoth runtime packages pull in `@struktoai/mirage-core` automatically.\n\n### CLI\n\n```bash\nnpm install -g @struktoai/mirage-cli\n# or\nuvx --from mirage-ai mirage\n# or\nnpx @struktoai/mirage-cli\n```\n\nTo get started, see the quickstarts for\n[Python](https://docs.mirage.strukto.ai/python/quickstart),\n[TypeScript](https://docs.mirage.strukto.ai/typescript/quickstart) and the\n[CLI](https://docs.mirage.strukto.ai/home/access/cli).\n\n## Scriptable Policy\n\nA profile can name policy scripts for what its rules cannot express. A script's\n`pre_command` takes the command, can open the files it names, and returns a\ndeny, an ask or `None`. This one disables `rm`, and a Python script whose code\ndeletes files:\n\n```python\ndef deletes(path):\n    try:\n        code = open(path).read()\n    except OSError:\n        return False\n    return any(call in code for call in (\"os.remove\", \"os.unlink\", \"shutil.rmtree\"))\n\n\ndef pre_command(ctx):\n    if ctx[\"command\"] == \"rm\" or (\n        ctx[\"command\"].startswith(\"python\") and any(deletes(p) for p in ctx[\"paths\"])\n    ):\n        return {\"kind\": \"deny\", \"reason\": \"deleting files is disabled\"}\n```\n\nRegister it in a profile, here to run on Monty before every command:\n\n```python\nws = Workspace(\n    {\"/s3\": (S3VFS(S3Config(bucket=\"my-bucket\")), MountMode.WRITE)},\n    profiles={\n        \"analyst\": {\n            \"policy\": {\n                \"pre_command\": [{\"script\": ScriptSource(Path(\"guard.py\").read_text()), \"runtime\": \"monty\"}],\n            },\n        },\n    },\n    profile=\"analyst\",\n)\n```\n\n```console\n$ cat /s3/clean.py\nimport os\nos.remove(\"/s3/report.txt\")\n$ rm /s3/report.txt\nrm: Permission denied\n$ python3 /s3/clean.py\npython3: Permission denied\n```\n\nSee [policy scripts](https://docs.mirage.strukto.ai/home/policy/scripts) for\nthe other stages a script can answer at.\n\n## Embedded Terminal\n\nMost of the time an agent does not need a sandbox, only a terminal-like\ninterface, and Mirage embeds one in an application server. Each terminal is a\nMirage session with its own working directory, environment and history, and Python\nruns in-process on Monty, so a terminal starts with no container or VM. Here\nit is in Express; the FastAPI version is in the\n[docs](https://docs.mirage.strukto.ai/home/examples/embedded-terminal).\n\n```bash\nnpm install @struktoai/mirage-node @pydantic/monty express\n```\n\n```ts\nimport express from 'express'\nimport { MontyRuntime, MountMode, RAMVFS, Workspace } from '@struktoai/mirage-node'\n\nconst ws = new Workspace(\n  { '/work': new RAMVFS() },\n  { mode: MountMode.EXEC, runtimes: [new MontyRuntime({ captures: ['python', 'python3'] })] },\n)\nconst app = express()\napp.use(express.json())\n\napp.post('/sessions/:id', (req, res) => {\n  ws.createSession(req.params.id)\n  res.sendStatus(201)\n})\n\napp.post('/sessions/:id/run', async (req, res) => {\n  const r = await ws.shell(req.body.command, { sessionId: req.params.id })\n  res.json({ stdout: r.stdoutText, stderr: r.stderrText, exitCode: r.exitCode })\n})\n\napp.listen(3000, '127.0.0.1')\n```\n\n## Contributors\n\nThanks to everyone who has contributed to Mirage.\n\n<a href=\"https://github.com/strukto-ai/mirage/graphs/contributors\">\n  <img src=\"https://contrib.rocks/image?repo=strukto-ai/mirage\" alt=\"Mirage contributors\" />\n</a>\n"
